{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Rav lakhem, sons of Levi.</b> I have said a great thing to you. And they were not fools — so how could he warn them thus and they accepted it upon themselves to draw near? They sinned against their own lives, as it says ״אֵת מַחְתּוֹת הַחַטָּאִים הָאֵלֶּה בְּנַפְשֹׁתָם״ (Numbers 17:3). And Korah, who was a sharp man — what did he see in this folly? His eye misled him: he saw that a great chain would come forth from him — Samuel, who is equivalent to Moses and Aaron. He said: For his sake I escape. And twenty-four watches stand for his descendants, all of them prophesying by the holy spirit, as it says ״כָּל אֵלֶּה בָּנִים לְהֵימָן״ (I Chronicles 25:5). He said: Is it possible that all this greatness is destined to arise from me, and I should be lost? Therefore he joined to come into that confrontation, for he heard from the mouth of Moses that all of them perish and one escapes — ״אֲשֶׁר יִבְחַר ה' הוּא הַקָּדוֹשׁ.״ He erred and hung it upon himself, and did not see clearly — because his sons repented, and Moses saw this. — Tanchuma." "<b>Rav lakhem.</b> You have taken upon yourselves a great matter — to oppose the Holy One, blessed be He."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The לקריב in the first sentence reads anomalously; rendered as 'to draw near,' reading it as referring to Korah's faction accepting the test of the fire-pans. The phrase וכ״ד משמרות is abbreviated for twenty-four (כ\"ד)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:16.057960854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}